      "created_at": "2018-07-16T15:43:19Z",
      "updated_at": "2018-07-16T15:43:19Z",
      "body": "Session idle timeout is definitely an important factor when securing sensitive data - especially now when the new EU law on data protection and privacy has come into play.\r\nWe are hoping to start up with nextcloud this fall and are having some trouble as well with session lifetime. As jospoortvliet is mentioning, Nextcloud are having a notification pooling / heartbeat happening every 30 sec that possibly is keeping the session active even though the session are meant to expire. Practically when session lifetime is configured to 29 seconds in nextcloud's config.php file like this:\r\n\r\n'remember_login_cookie_lifetime' => 0,\r\n'session_lifetime' => 29,\r\n'session_keepalive' => false\r\n\r\nusers are being logged out after 29 seconds. But when it is set to 30 or more - users are not being logged out.\r\n\r\nThis is, for us, a huge security concern when working around unauthorized people every minute of the day with laptops.",
      "author_association": "NONE",
      "pin": null,
